   "prompt": "A cosy Japanese lo-fi hip hop song for studying late at night, warm and dreamy, from the same world as a bittersweet anime ending. Slow laid-back boom-bap groove around 76 BPM with dusty swung drums, soft rimshots and a round muffled kick. Mellow Rhodes electric piano playing jazzy seventh and ninth chords, a warm upright-style bass, a gentle nylon guitar motif and faint vinyl crackle with soft rain outside a window. A soft, close, breathy female vocal sings in Japanese, relaxed and intimate, almost whispered in the verses and a little brighter in the hook, with light doubled harmonies. Begin with rain, crackle and the Rhodes alone like a desk lamp switching on. Keep the verses sparse and steady. Let the hook float with a simple, memorable melody. Leave a short instrumental break where the Rhodes and guitar trade a tiny melody over the beat. End with the beat dropping out, the Rhodes and the rain fading together. Tape-saturated warm mix, gentle low-pass filtering, soft reverb, no spoken dialogue, no crowd noise, no abrupt ending.",
   "lyrics": "[intro]\n[RAIN, VINYL CRACKLE AND SOFT RHODES]\n\n[verse]\n窓の向こう　雨のリズム\nノートの端に　小さな落書き\nあたたかいお茶　湯気がゆれて\n時計の針も　ゆっくり歩く\n\nヘッドフォンの中　やさしい夜\n眠い目こすって　ページをめくる\n街の灯りが　にじんで見える\nまだ少しだけ　ここにいたい\n\n[chorus]\nゆっくりでいいよ　急がなくていい\n今夜の音に　包まれて\n明日のことは　明日に任せて\nこのページだけ　読み終えよう\n\n[instrumental]\n[RHODES AND NYLON GUITAR MELODY OVER THE BEAT]\n\n[verse]\n消しゴムのかす　机の上\n書きかけの夢　まだ途中でも\nしっぽをまるめて　深呼吸して\nひとつずつでいい　前に進む\n\n[chorus]\nゆっくりでいいよ　急がなくていい\n今夜の音に　包まれて\n明日のことは　明日に任せて\nこのページだけ　読み終えよう\n\n[outro]\n雨がやむころ　またね\nおやすみ　やさしい夜\n\n[BEAT FADES, RHODES AND RAIN LINGER]",
   "drop": 21.25,
